  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri Penumalla Suresh vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 3",
    "facts": "The case of prosecution is that the Inspector of Police, II] Town Police Station, Visakhapatnam City on 02.07.2020 found one person going on TVS Motor cycle on seeing the police, he tried to escape. Then the police caught hold of the said person and asked about the details and confessed by A-3 the police searched and found tobacco products like Gutkha, Khainee etc., in the name of brand Gokul Deluxe tobacco, Meeraj etc., and also seized 4 KGs of Ganja in two packets. Basing on that, the crime was registered.",
    "arguments": "4. The learned counsel for the petitioner submits that in respect of other crimes under IPC, COTP Act and FSS Act, this Court has already [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings in FIR No.588 of 2020 vide order dated 22.07.2020 in Crl.P.No.2767 of 2020. Learned counsel further submits that as far as the offence punishable under NDPS Act is concerned, the contraband seized from the accused is 4 KGs which is not a commercial quantity, as such prays for grant of bail to the petitioner.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. The learned counsel for the petitioner submits that in respect of other crimes under IPC, COTP Act and FSS Act, this Court has already [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings in FIR No.588 of 2020 vide order dated 22.07.2020 in Crl.P.No.2767 of 2020. Learned counsel further submits that as far as the offence punishable under NDPS Act is concerned, the contraband seized from the accused is 4 KGs which is not a commercial quantity, as such prays for grant of bail to the petitioner.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
